I have just finished playing one of the most unlucky games ever!

I was playing a human N Arch named Art, and doing sort of Ok for a while. 
I found a wand - Secret Door Detection (thanks, RNG), and had a doggie who
was doing kinda well...  I made it down to DL5 (heading to Sokoban) when 2
things happened in quick succession, radically changing my situation for
the worse.

First, doggie disappeared, victim to a level-teleporter.  No problem,
right?  I'll just go hunt for him...oh, Crap - a bunch of Killer Bees! 
I decided discretion was the better part of valour, and ran...but the only
place I had to run was downstairs - they'd cut me off from the up-stairs.

Ok, I've survived these before.  I go down, and find a room with a hole in
it, and get set upon by a horde of rothes...  In no shape to deal with
this, I am forced to retreat yet LOWER into the dungeon, where I promptly
get 1, hallucination, and 2, blinded.  I end up eating most of my food
waiting to deal with reality...  After much running around, trying to get
rothes to fall into a hole, dancing with a nymph on a bones level, and 
running away, away, away, I finally make it back to the killer bees.  Not
willing to go deeper in, I resorted to giving them the finger - i.e., the
E-word...  Not too effective, but I managed to retreat still further up
the dungeon.

I now had a mostly used wand of magic missle, a sling and rocks, and JUNK.
 My AC was maybe 2.  I decided the mines were my only choice...especially
as I was starting to get hungry!  Of course, they were dark, and I had no
light source, but I managed to satisfy my hunger for a while, found two
oh-so-useful whistles, went deeper in, and got blinded...again.  I ran
into a pack of rothes while blind, killed one, and ran from the other two
when I got my sight back - I had 1 hp, and was running for the stairs.  I
*still* had *NOTHING* useful.

A fox showed up out of the darkness, and before I could do anything, put
Art out of his misery...

I really thought I'd pull him off - he'd made it out of so many scrapes! 
But who was I kidding, really?  At least he left a totally worthless bones
file...

